{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgOps","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NormalForms","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Image"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.mkDegLexOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.mkDegLexOrder","kind":"def","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/AlgOps.lean#L107-L205","doc":"Construct a deg-lex `AdmissibleOrder` for any generator type `G`\nequipped with an injective rank function `rank : G → ℕ`.\n\nThis generalises `degLexOrder` from NormalForms.lean (which is\nspecific to `SU2Gen`).  The proofs are identical in structure:\n- Well-foundedness: from `List.Lex.wellFounded` via rank\n- Trichotomy: case split on length, then on lex\n- Compatibility: length preserved by concatenation\n\nWe delegate to the existing NormalForms infrastructure by mapping\ngenerators to `SU2Gen` (or more precisely, to `ℕ` via rank) and\nusing `List.Lex.wellFounded` directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.shortLex_wellFounded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.shortLex_wellFounded","kind":"theorem","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/AlgOps.lean#L30-L105","doc":"**Shortlex well-foundedness** (Mathlib v4.24.0 gap). Pure `List.Lex` is *not*\nwell-founded on unbounded-length lists (e.g. `[1] ≻ [0,1] ≻ [0,0,1] ≻ …`); the\nlength-first refinement — \"shorter word, or equal length and lexicographically\nsmaller\" — restores well-foundedness for any well-founded base relation `r`.\nThis is the generic replacement for `NormalForms.lexEncoding`, whose fixed-base\nencoding into `ℕ` only works for the finite generator set `SU2Gen`; an arbitrary\ninjective `rank : G → ℕ` has unbounded image, so no order-embedding of the\nlength-`n` lex order (order type `ω^n`) into `ℕ` (order type `ω`) exists — the\naccessibility must be proved directly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}